This empty file tells GitHub Pages to serve the repository as plain static
files instead of running it through Jekyll.

Why it matters here:
- The site is plain HTML/CSS/JS, so Jekyll processing adds nothing.
- Jekyll silently skips files and folders whose names begin with "_" or ".".
  Without this file, any such asset added later would 404 on the live site.
- Builds finish faster and cannot fail on Jekyll parsing errors.
